     "explanation": "Holiday explicitly defines ego as **an unhealthy belief in your own importance** — the inflated gap between what you actually are and what you believe yourself to be. He is careful to distinguish ego from confidence (which is grounded in evidence), ambition (which can be humble), and self-esteem (which is stable and quiet). He also explicitly avoids the Freudian definition. The 'gap' framing is central to the book.",
