     "explanation": "Belichick went **back to being an assistant** under Bill Parcells. From the outside, this looked like demotion. From his inside scorecard, it was continuity — the same standards, the same work, now with hard-won failure data to incorporate. Holiday's emphasis is that Belichick didn't reinvent himself, didn't change paths, didn't perform a comeback narrative. He kept executing the same disciplines. The dynasty 5+ years later was built on the unchanged inside scorecard.",
