     "explanation": "Holiday uses the phrase specifically for **hard time** — the stretches after a loss, in a constrained situation, or during forced waiting. Alive time and dead time are not different activities; they are the **same hours** experienced under a different internal relationship. Malcolm X's prison hours were dead time for most around him and alive time for him. Disney's train ride home from losing Oswald was dead time for most former founders; he sketched Mickey Mouse. The external situation is identical; the internal use is opposite.",
