    {
     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Practice: The First Principles Sealing",
     "content": "**Time: 60 minutes. Materials: notebook + a physical envelope or sealed file.**\n\nThis practice is your defense against the **terrible advice failure gives**. You're going to write your first principles down NOW — in a calm season — and seal them, so that during a future failure you can return to them rather than rewriting them.\n\n**Step 1 — Write your six first principles.**\nUse the categories from the lesson:\n1. What kind of work I do — quality level, ethics\n2. How I treat people — colleagues, opponents, family\n3. What I won't sell out for — money, status, attention, fear\n4. What I owe my future self — health, learning, integrity\n5. What I owe people who depend on me\n6. The lines I will not cross even if I lose for it\n\nWrite each one as a short, declarative sentence in your own voice. Not corporate, not aspirational. *I do not ship work I would be embarrassed to put my name on. I do not throw colleagues under the bus. I do not trade my health for short-term wins.*\n\n**Step 2 — Add three 'never even in failure' lines.**\nAnticipate that failure will offer you trades. Pre-decide what you will not trade away. Examples:\n• *Even if my project fails, I will not blame the team publicly.*\n• *Even if my book bombs, I will not write the next one to chase the market.*\n• *Even if I lose this job, I will not take a role that violates my ethics for short-term cash.*\n\n**Step 3 — Sign and seal.**\nLiterally — sign the document, fold it, put it in an envelope marked **'open in the next significant failure.'** Or, if digital, create a file you'll commit to not editing for at least 6 months.\n\n**Step 4 — Schedule the unsealing.**\nThis is the deliberate trigger: the next time you experience a meaningful loss, you will physically open this document **before** you make any significant decisions. Re-read it. Sit with it for 24 hours before changing any major principle.\n\n**Why this works:** Most of the damage failure does is through fast, post-loss decisions made when ego's bad advice sounds reasonable. The sealed document is a pre-commitment. Your past, calmer self gets one more vote in the room when failure tries to rewrite the rules.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">FIRST PRINCIPLES SEALING</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">A vote from your calmer self</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"190\" width=\"940\" height=\"180\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"240\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">STEP 1 — WRITE YOUR 6 PRINCIPLES</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"285\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Work. People. Won't-sell-out. Future self.</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"320\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Dependents. Lines you will not cross.</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"355\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Short declarative sentences. Your voice.</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"390\" width=\"940\" height=\"220\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"440\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">STEP 2 — THREE \"EVEN IN FAILURE\" LINES</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">\"Even if project fails, won't blame team publicly.\"</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"520\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">\"Even if book bombs, won't chase market.\"</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"555\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">\"Even if I lose this job, won't violate ethics for cash.\"</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"590\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Pre-decide what failure cannot trade away.</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"630\" width=\"940\" height=\"160\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"680\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">STEP 3 — SIGN AND SEAL</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"725\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Envelope: \"Open in next significant failure.\"</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"760\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Digital? Lock the file. No edits for 6 months.</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"810\" width=\"940\" height=\"160\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"860\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">STEP 4 — SCHEDULE THE UNSEALING</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"905\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Open BEFORE making any big post-loss decision.</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"940\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Sit 24 hours. Then act — or don't.</text>\n                </svg>",
      "caption": "Your calmer self in the room when failure arrives"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "application",
     "title": "Apply This Today: Three Always-Love Moves",
     "content": "**1. Identify one current 'dead time' in your life.** Even small ones count — a commute, a recovery period, a stretch between projects, the boring weeks of a long task. Name it. Pick **one specific use** you will give that time this week. A podcast becomes a reading hour. A waiting room becomes a writing session. A recovery week becomes deliberate fundamentals practice. The clock is the same. **You** change.\n\n**2. Reaffirm one first principle out loud.** Pick one of your standards — a quality level, an ethical line, a way you treat people — and reaffirm it in a specific situation this week. Even if nobody else sees. The point is the **internal contract**, renewed. Ego erodes principles silently; you reaffirm them deliberately.\n\n**3. Refuse one piece of bitterness disguised as wisdom.** Notice the last cynical line you accepted as 'realism.' *People only care about themselves. The system is rigged. Nobody reads anymore. Nice guys finish last.* Pick one. Ask: is this real, or is this an old wound speaking? Replace it with a more precise sentence. The new sentence may sound naive. **Naive is sometimes more accurate than bitter.**\n\nAll three moves are forms of amor fati — loving what is rather than fighting it. None require anything to change externally. All begin to **reverse the spiral that real failure starts** before it has a chance to deepen.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">THREE MOVES TODAY</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Daily forms of amor fati</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"200\" width=\"940\" height=\"240\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"255\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">1. CONVERT ONE DEAD TIME</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"305\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">A commute, a wait, a recovery week.</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"345\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Give it one specific use this week.</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"395\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Same clock. Different you.</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"460\" width=\"940\" height=\"240\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"515\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">2. REAFFIRM ONE PRINCIPLE</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"565\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Pick a standard. Live it this week.</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"605\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Even if nobody sees.</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"655\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">The internal contract, renewed.</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"720\" width=\"940\" height=\"240\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"775\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">3. REFUSE ONE CYNICISM</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"825\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">\"Nobody reads anymore.\" Real, or wound?</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"865\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Replace with a more precise sentence.</text>\n                    <text x=\"130\" y=\"915\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Naive is sometimes more accurate than bitter.</text>\n                </svg>",
      "caption": "Three small refusals of the failure spiral"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quote",
     "content": "Of course you should do everything you can to avoid disaster — but never to forget the role suffering plays in shaping who we are and what we can become.",
     "author": "Ryan Holiday",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">WISDOM</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Avoidance and acceptance, both true</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"280\" width=\"940\" height=\"500\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.1)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"370\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-style=\"italic\" font-size=\"26\">\"Of course you should</text>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"415\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-style=\"italic\" font-size=\"26\">do everything you can</text>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"460\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-style=\"italic\" font-size=\"26\">to avoid disaster —</text>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"540\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-style=\"italic\" font-size=\"26\">but never to forget</text>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"585\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-style=\"italic\" font-size=\"26\">the role suffering plays</text>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"630\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-style=\"italic\" font-size=\"26\">in shaping who we are</text>\n                    <text x=\"120\" y=\"710\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-style=\"italic\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"30\">and who we can become.\"</text>\n                    <text x=\"980\" y=\"760\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-size=\"22\">— Ryan Holiday</text>\n                    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"810\" width=\"940\" height=\"150\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.08)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"860\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\">Avoid the loss. Use the loss.</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"900\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Both are forms of taking it seriously.</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"940\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Neither requires loving the loss itself.</text>\n                </svg>",
      "caption": "Avoid disaster. Use what disaster cannot avoid."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "Holiday says you should make no major principle changes for how long after a significant loss?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "Immediately — the loss is the lesson, act on it now",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Roughly 90 days — sit with the pain, run the AAR, but don't rewrite values while the wound is fresh",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "10 years — until you've completely processed the failure",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Never — principles should be reconsidered weekly regardless",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Holiday's discipline is specifically the **90-day rule** for principle changes after meaningful failure. You should adjust specific tactics where the data clearly demands it (the AAR). You should not rewrite your **values** while the wound is fresh, because failure is a terrible teacher of new values — bitterness disguises itself as wisdom, and counterfactuals about 'what if I'd cut corners' are unreliable. The discipline is to sit with the pain, run precise tactical reviews, and leave principles alone for ~90 days.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">The 90-day rule</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"220\" width=\"900\" height=\"240\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"280\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">FAILURE IS A BAD TEACHER OF VALUES</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"335\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Bitterness disguises itself as wisdom.</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"380\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Counterfactuals are unreliable.</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"425\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Loss narrows perception toward fast relief.</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"500\" width=\"900\" height=\"220\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"555\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">THE DISCIPLINE</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"605\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Run the AAR. Adjust tactics.</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"645\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Leave principles alone for ~90 days.</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"690\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Reconsider later with distance, in calm season.</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"760\" width=\"900\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"815\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">DON'T BURN THE HOUSE</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"860\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">to fix one room.</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"905\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Your principles built whatever standing remains.</text>\n                </svg>",
      "caption": "Leave values alone while the wound is fresh"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "What is the deepest version of 'amor fati' Holiday describes?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "Believing every bad thing secretly happened for your benefit",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Loving the time and circumstance you actually have, even when you didn't choose them — and refusing to spend that time asleep at the wheel",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "Becoming emotionally numb so that nothing can hurt you",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Convincing yourself that suffering is enjoyable",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Holiday is careful: amor fati is **not** the claim that everything happens for the best (option 1), nor numbness (option 3), nor self-deception (option 4). It is the disciplined refusal to **waste the time you actually have**, even when the situation was not chosen. Malcolm in prison didn't 'love' the unjust sentence. He refused to be asleep at the wheel of the hours he was given. That distinction — between loving the event and loving the use of one's response to it — is the version Holiday actually preaches.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">The deepest form of amor fati</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"220\" width=\"900\" height=\"220\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"280\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">NOT</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"330\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">\"Everything happens for the best.\"</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"370\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">\"Suffering is enjoyable.\"</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"410\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Self-deception is not the practice.</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"480\" width=\"900\" height=\"280\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"540\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">YES</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"595\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Love the time you actually have.</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"640\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Refuse to be asleep at the wheel of it.</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">The event was not chosen.</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"730\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Your relationship to it is.</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"800\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"855\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">THE MALCOLM DISTINCTION</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"900\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Not loving the sentence.</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"935\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Refusing to waste the hours.</text>\n                </svg>",
      "caption": "Love the response, not the event"
     }
    }
