     "explanation": "Holiday's most important honesty — and the central reason his book ends with practices rather than principles — is that **ego is never defeated permanently**. You will not finish this seminar a permanently humble person. The voice will return tomorrow, in a new costume. The work is **practices, not insights**: a daily audit, a Standard of Performance, a set of truth-tellers, a sealed first-principles document, a way of treating dead time. That's why the capstone is an integrated 90-day cycle rather than a final realization.",
