     "explanation": "Holiday is precise: ego-defeating work is **invisible by design**. If you perform humility for an audience — posting about how humble you're becoming, broadcasting the practice, fishing for praise — you have **simply moved ego to a different tank** (humble-image ego instead of accomplishment ego). The whole point of the audit, the canvas strategy, the standard of performance, and the sealed first principles is that they work in private. Nobody applauds. That privacy IS the discipline. Performing them defeats the purpose.",
