     "explanation": "The two tests Holiday actually points to throughout Parts II and III: (1) **the no-audience test** — would you still keep the standard, do the work, hold the line, if nobody were watching? and (2) **the old peer test** — does the person who knew you before the wins say you're still you afterward? Both of these are **internal-scorecard** measures. They are explicitly NOT about follower counts, feelings of confidence, or being publicly recognized as humble — all of which would be reintroducing the outside scorecard through a side door.",
